Build 031 (from the 030 run, the user's request for no vertex explosions and CPU work, AnyPS5's rules):
- Mesh draws with a task program are skipped by default and counted (EDEN_MESH_DRAW_DROPPED task);
  /data/eden-nx2/task-draws-on.txt (EDEN_NX2_TASK_DRAWS) runs them again. Their emulation drew the
  vertex explosions (gone whenever these draws were: 025 mesh-draws-off, 026b task programs rejected).
  It also stops allocating the 64-128 MiB task output arenas. Known gap: what they drew is missing.
- VMA device-memory blocks are 16 MiB on the PS5 (EDEN_NX2_VMA_BLOCK_MIB, vma-block-mib.txt; 64
  before): 529-907 MiB sat free inside partly used 64 MiB blocks when the pool ran out (026-030).
- EDEN_SUBMIT_DEPTH (stdout/heap.log every 5 s): how many submissions the GPU had not finished at
  each submit, and the submit call's time. The Vulkan worker spent ~92% of its time in vkQueueSubmit
  (~19.6 ms, ~2.4 per frame); depth tells CPU-bound (0) from GPU-bound (1+) before any optimization.

